<|im_start|>user
Problem: In a village of 12 mathematicians, each belonging to either the $\sqrt{2}$-clan or the $\pi$-clan, every mathematician has an odd number of friends, and each has a birthday in a different month. On their birthday, each mathematician switches to the majority clan among their friends. Let $N$ be the minimum number of months after which no mathematician changes their clan. Find the value of $N$.

Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
<|im_start|>assistant


Completion:
<think>
Okay, so I have this problem about mathematicians in a village with 12 people, each from either the √2-clan or the π-clan. Each mathematician has an odd number of friends, and each has a birthday in a different month. On their birthday, they switch to the majority clan among their friends. I need to find the minimum number of months N after which no mathematician changes their clan. 

